+Generated with the built-in image generation tool. No reference images were used.
+
+85-pompeii-fresco.png
+
+Create one fresh image solely from this text, square 1024x1024. An ancient Roman Pompeii fresco covering the entire image: a broad architectural wall painting in Pompeian red, with slender trompe-l'oeil columns and painted niches, faded mineral pigments sunk into lime plaster, irregular cracks and areas of missing plaster revealing the rough substrate. The composition is a wide Roman wall scene, with a small elegant FULL-BODY seated woman inside one architectural bay, ample red wall and fictive architecture around her. She is in her early 30s, has curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater; render these modern character attributes entirely using ancient fresco brushwork and ochre pigments. She enjoys coffee from a simple clay cup raised gracefully toward her lips, and a crescent croissant rests nearby on a little painted pedestal table. Roman figural anatomy, flowing painted contours, restrained modeled earth-pigment shading, relaxed classical seated pose and incomplete surviving details. Prioritize a convincing authentic Pompeian fresco artifact and its architectural organization over portrait accuracy. Matte abraded paint, not oil painting; no contemporary photographic person, no filter aesthetic. Square edge-to-edge fresco fragment with no museum surround. No text, letters, captions, signatures, or watermarks. Do not use any reference image.
+
+86-aztec-codex.png
+
+Create one fresh image solely from this text, square 1024x1024. A pre-Columbian Aztec codex painting on fibrous warm tan bark paper: a strongly stylized PROFILE figure with an oversized angular head and compact folded limbs, seated on a simple mat, facing right and enjoying coffee in a decorated bowl-like cup. This is a planar pictorial manuscript composition, no optical perspective, no photographic anatomy, no lighting or rendered depth. The character is a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair rendered as red-brown stepped curls, freckles as a few painted cheek dots, round tortoiseshell glasses shown as a patterned circular frame in profile, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater rendered as an ochre flat shape with small graphic stitch patterns. A clearly recognizable crescent croissant sits next to her on a shallow dish. Bold black hand-painted outlines, flat turquoise, red and ochre pigment blocks, deliberate angular anatomy and very simplified hands. Organize the scene asymmetrically across the bark paper with a few glyph-like ABSTRACT geometric ornaments that are purely invented nonlinguistic shapes, not real glyphs and not a writing system. Visible paper fibers and slight pigment abrasion. Authentic codex visual grammar must dictate proportions and spacing, no modern cartoon or generic fantasy illustration. No text, real glyphs, letters, captions, signatures or watermarks. Do not use any reference image.
+
+87-madhubani.png
+
+Create one fresh image solely from this text, square 1024x1024. An intricate Indian Madhubani folk painting made with bright natural pigments and fine black ink on handmade paper. Dense all-over double-line outlines filled with tiny hatching, dots, parallel strokes and fine patterns, with fish, birds, flowers, stems and patterned leaves filling EVERY surrounding space. Use an emphatic intimate waist-up frontal decorative figure, large almond eyes, flat stylized face and a tilted head, asymmetric arms forming an ornamental shape around a coffee cup she enjoys holding close to her mouth. She is a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair as coiling reddish-brown patterned locks, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses with patterned rims, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater filled with meticulously drawn rhythmic stitch motifs. A clearly recognizable croissant on a small plate appears nearby within the dense foreground ornament. Flat symbolic Madhubani proportions and linework, absolutely no realism, no gradients, no cast shadows and no photographic perspective. Saffron yellow, vermilion, leaf green, deep blue, black and warm paper white, all as natural pigment color areas. Layered dense geometric floral borders integrated into the whole composition; no empty space anywhere. The folk painting style is the priority and determines every mark. No text, letters, captions, signatures or watermarks. Do not use any reference image.
+
+88-delft-tile.png
+
+Create one fresh image solely from this text, square 1024x1024. A hand-painted Delft blue ceramic tile panel, exactly four by four square tiles filling the square image edge to edge, with visible subtly uneven pale grout lines. Authentic cobalt-blue painting on milky white tin glaze, delicate hand-brushed contours and transparent cobalt washes, little traditional floral corner ornaments and subtle glossy glaze reflections. A continuous picturesque Dutch windmill landscape painted across the tile grid: windmill, low distant houses, canal banks, little bridge, airy clouds and reeds. In the foreground at the right, a woman sits SIDE-ON at a tiny outdoor table drinking coffee while watching the landscape, full seated figure integrated at a modest scale into the scenery rather than dominating the panel. A clearly recognizable croissant is on her table. The character is a woman in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, and a mustard-yellow knit sweater. Because authentic Delft monochrome is the priority, translate ALL her colors, hair and sweater included, into cobalt-blue linework, dots and patterned washes on white glaze: no actual yellow, brown or multicolor accents. Show knit ribs and curls with delicate cobalt brush marks and the glasses as patterned round frames. Style determines anatomy, pose, scale and old-fashioned landscape perspective. The woman is visibly hand-painted ceramic decoration, never a photographic human. Front-on view of the whole tile panel with discreet physical glaze shine and slight craquelure, no room or frame surrounding it. No text, letters, captions, signatures or watermarks. Do not use any reference image.

